{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "cf4861561cec4d8d90187c793d573e02",
    "m_Title": "How this Works",
    "m_Content": "First we take a float (strength) invert it so the value adjusts intuitively. \n\nApply the strength to the fresnel effect.\n\nStep the fresnel effect to make a hard step with no blur.\n\nBool check if the hard step is desired. Multiply the bool by the effect to turn it on. \n(true = on/false = off) If we think about it in math and 1 = true, 0 = false then multiplying by 1 = 1 = on and multiplying by 0 = 0 = off. So if its on its ON.\n\nThe weird one is when checking if its OFF to reapply the blurred effect. we used a Remap node with these specific values and it works as needed. It inverts the bool value of 1 to 0 and 0 to 1 which allows us to use it for false instead of true. \n\nSo if hardstep is OFF the blurred edges is true.\n\nFinally we add the two values so neither affects the other like it would with multiply.\n\n\n",
    "m_TextSize": 0,
    "m_Theme": 0,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": -2288.0,
        "y": -319.0,
        "width": 838.0,
        "height": 251.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": ""
    }
}

